{"meta":{"format_version":"4.10","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"maul_stone","model_identifier":"maul_stone","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"# maul_stone\n\nStone maul (stone tools: made at the Big House, no research)\n\n- The rock breaker: a rounded river cobble with a groove pecked round its middle, the thick wooden handle bound into the groove with cord. Blunt at both ends, battered striking faces; nothing like the pointed metal pickaxe. Used for quarrying and breaking rock until metal picks.\n- Two-handed, about 85 cm. Same frame as the catalogue's `pick`: grip at the origin, head at the -Z end, main striking face on -Y. Held at `slot_hand_r`; plays the worker's `mine` clip.\n- Warm speckled grey granite, hide lashing. 10 cubes, texture 32 x 64. No clips.\n"},"resolution":{"width":32,"height":64},"elements":[{"name":"haft","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"light_emission":0,"render_order":"default","allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[-0.8,-0.9,-24.0],"to":[0.8,0.9,3.5],"autouv":0,"color":0,"inflate":0.0,"origin":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[16,42,17.6,43.8],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[16,42,17.6,43.8],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[0,40,27.5,41.8],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[0,40,27.5,41.8],"texture":0},"up":{"uv":[0,0,1.6,27.5],"texture":0},"down":{"uv":[0,0,1.6,27.5],"texture":0}},"type":"cube","uuid":"a2e4cfe3-3250-50ee-a001-3c6948ef8085"},{"name":"haft_end","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"light_emission":0,"render_order":"default","allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[-1.0,-1.1,3.5],"to":[1.0,1.1,4.5],"autouv":0,"color":0,"inflate":0.0,"origin":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[10,37,12.0,39.2],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[10,37,12.0,39.2],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[16,37,17.0,39.2],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[16,37,17.0,39.2],"texture":0},"up":{"uv":[28,42,30.0,43.0],"texture":0},"down":{"uv":[28,42,